I tend to explore downwards until I've collected enough
that one more item makes me burdened then shuttle the
loot up to my stash or move my stash down.  Depends on
whether I'm polypiling just how much I move.

With the W or V Quest artifact I tend to explore
downwards even while Burdened ready to drop the bag
for combat.  Then the first item that pushes me past
burdened I'll level teleort to my stash, drop the loot
and head down again.

Early on I start digging out direct paths on each
level so a cruise down from my stash is a fast trip
toward unexplored levels.  A level with a lot of loot
like the two castles can take a lot of shuttling trips.
Most other levels average 1-2 trips per level.  Passing
through level after level in quick succession gives me
enough monsters that I stay Satiated much of the time
once I've gotten all of the intrinsics and it also
ensures that I am well healed and safe to pray during
most exploration phases.  It does take a vast number of
game turns, part of my tendency to be over-prepared.


